  "subSubTitle": "Go beyond limits and create without boundaries.",
  "tips_article_1_subtitle": "Define the main subject and decide exactly what readers should understand, learn, or take away from the article.",
  "tips_article_1_title": "Mulai dengan topik yang jelas",
  "tips_article_2_subtitle": "Introduce the topic quickly, explain why it matters, and give readers a clear idea of what they will learn.",
  "tips_article_2_title": "Tulis pendahuluan yang kuat",
  "tips_article_3_subtitle": "Arrange information logically so each section supports the main topic and naturally leads into the next.",
  "tips_article_3_title": "Susun ide Anda",
  "tips_article_4_subtitle": "Prefer straightforward sentences and explain technical ideas when writing for readers who may not know the topic.",
  "tips_article_4_title": "Gunakan bahasa yang jelas",
  "tips_article_5_subtitle": "Use examples, explanations, comparisons, facts, or evidence whenever they help readers understand an important idea.",
  "tips_article_5_title": "Dukung poin penting",
  "tips_article_6_subtitle": "Summarize the main message and leave readers with a useful takeaway, recommendation, or final thought.",
  "tips_article_6_title": "Akhiri dengan kuat",
  "tips_article_reminder": "Good articles respect the reader's time. Make every paragraph useful, clear, and connected to the main topic.",
  "tips_article_subtitle": "Create informative and engaging articles with strong structure, clear ideas, useful details, and easy-to-read writing.",
  "tips_article_title": "Tips Menulis Artikel",
  "tips_book_1_subtitle": "Outline the beginning, major turning points, climax, and ending so the overall direction of your book remains clear.",
  "tips_book_1_title": "Rencanakan alur utama",
  "tips_book_2_subtitle": "Allow personalities, relationships, motivations, conflicts, and character growth to develop naturally across chapters.",
  "tips_book_2_title": "Kembangkan karakter secara bertahap",
  "tips_book_3_subtitle": "Give each chapter a clear purpose and end key chapters with tension, discovery, or a reason to keep reading.",
  "tips_book_3_title": "Susun bab dengan baik",
  "tips_book_4_subtitle": "Track timelines, locations, relationships, character traits, and previous events so the book remains consistent.",
  "tips_book_4_title": "Jaga kesinambungan",
  "tips_book_5_subtitle": "Balance action, dialogue, description, reflection, and major events so the book feels natural from beginning to end.",
  "tips_book_5_title": "Atur tempo cerita",
  "tips_book_6_subtitle": "Allow earlier conflicts and character choices to naturally lead toward a conclusion that feels earned and satisfying.",
  "tips_book_6_title": "Bangun menuju akhir yang kuat",
  "tips_book_7_subtitle": "Review the completed book for repetition, inconsistencies, unnecessary scenes, weak transitions, and unclear dialogue.",
  "tips_book_7_title": "Edit dan sempurnakan",
  "tips_book_reminder": "Great books become stronger through revision. Keep the larger story consistent while making every chapter meaningful.",
  "tips_book_subtitle": "Plan your book carefully so the plot, chapters, characters, and overall progression remain consistent and engaging.",
  "tips_book_title": "Tips Menulis Buku",
  "tips_category_article": "Artikel",
  "tips_category_book": "Buku",
  "tips_category_letter": "Surat",
  "tips_category_lyrics": "Lirik",
  "tips_category_poem": "Puisi",
  "tips_category_screenplay": "Skenario",
  "tips_category_speech": "Pidato",
  "tips_category_story": "Cerita",
  "tips_letter_1_subtitle": "Be clear about why you are writing so the message remains focused and easy for the recipient to understand.",
  "tips_letter_1_title": "Pahami tujuan Anda",
  "tips_letter_2_subtitle": "Adjust your language, level of formality, emotional tone, and details based on your relationship with the reader.",
  "tips_letter_2_title": "Pertimbangkan penerima",
  "tips_letter_3_subtitle": "Choose a greeting that matches your relationship with the recipient and immediately establishes the right tone.",
  "tips_letter_3_title": "Mulai dengan tepat",
  "tips_letter_4_subtitle": "Organize your main points logically and avoid unnecessary details that distract from the purpose of the letter.",
  "tips_letter_4_title": "Jaga pesan tetap jelas",
  "tips_letter_5_subtitle": "When appropriate, include sincere details, feelings, or specific memories that make the letter feel genuine.",
  "tips_letter_5_title": "Tambahkan sentuhan pribadi",
  "tips_letter_6_subtitle": "Finish with a closing that matches the tone and leaves the recipient with a clear final impression.",
  "tips_letter_6_title": "Akhiri dengan tepat",
  "tips_letter_reminder": "The best letters feel intentional. Write for the person receiving the message and choose your tone based on your relationship.",
  "tips_letter_subtitle": "Write clear and thoughtful letters by matching your tone, structure, and message to the recipient and purpose.",
  "tips_letter_title": "Tips Menulis Surat",
  "tips_lyrics_1_subtitle": "Decide what your song is really about and keep verses, hooks, and emotional moments connected to that central idea.",
  "tips_lyrics_1_title": "Pahami tema utama",
  "tips_lyrics_2_subtitle": "Create a memorable phrase or chorus that captures the central emotion and remains easy for listeners to remember.",
  "tips_lyrics_2_title": "Tulis hook yang kuat",
  "tips_lyrics_3_subtitle": "Use natural wording, manageable line lengths, and phrases that feel comfortable when spoken or sung aloud.",
  "tips_lyrics_3_title": "Buat lirik mudah dinyanyikan",
  "tips_lyrics_4_subtitle": "Repeat important phrases enough to make them memorable without making the entire song feel repetitive.",
  "tips_lyrics_4_title": "Gunakan pengulangan dengan bijak",
  "tips_lyrics_5_subtitle": "Choose words and imagery that fit the genre, tempo, emotional tone, and atmosphere of the song.",
  "tips_lyrics_5_title": "Sesuaikan dengan suasana",
  "tips_lyrics_6_subtitle": "Use emotions and experiences listeners can recognize while still giving your lyrics a unique personality.",
  "tips_lyrics_6_title": "Buat mudah dipahami dan dirasakan",
  "tips_lyrics_reminder": "Read your lyrics aloud or imagine them with a melody. Words should not only look good on paper—they should feel natural when sung.",
  "tips_lyrics_subtitle": "Create memorable lyrics by combining emotion, rhythm, repetition, strong imagery, and a clear musical identity.",
  "tips_lyrics_title": "Tips Menulis Lirik",
  "tips_poem_1_subtitle": "Decide what feeling, experience, memory, or idea the poem should express before building your language around it.",
  "tips_poem_1_title": "Pilih emosi utama",
  "tips_poem_2_subtitle": "Use sensory details and visual language to help readers see, hear, feel, and imagine what you are describing.",
  "tips_poem_2_title": "Gunakan gambaran yang hidup",
  "tips_poem_3_subtitle": "Remove unnecessary words and focus on language that creates the strongest image, emotion, rhythm, or meaning.",
  "tips_poem_3_title": "Pilih kata dengan cermat",
  "tips_poem_4_subtitle": "Use line length, repetition, rhyme, meter, or free verse to create a flow that matches the emotion of the poem.",
  "tips_poem_4_title": "Bereksperimen dengan ritme",
  "tips_poem_5_subtitle": "Metaphors, similes, symbolism, and personification can transform simple ideas into richer emotional experiences.",
  "tips_poem_5_title": "Gunakan bahasa kiasan",
  "tips_poem_6_subtitle": "Finish with an image, realization, emotional shift, or thoughtful line that stays with the reader.",
  "tips_poem_6_title": "Ciptakan akhir yang bermakna",
  "tips_poem_reminder": "Poetry does not need many words to feel powerful. Strong imagery, rhythm, and genuine emotion often matter more than complexity.",
  "tips_poem_subtitle": "Use emotion, imagery, rhythm, and carefully chosen words to create poetry that feels expressive, personal, and memorable.",
  "tips_poem_title": "Tips Menulis Puisi",
  "tips_remember": "Ingat",
  "tips_screenplay_1_subtitle": "Describe actions and details that viewers can actually see or hear instead of explaining invisible internal thoughts.",
  "tips_screenplay_1_title": "Berpikir secara visual",
  "tips_screenplay_2_subtitle": "Each scene should develop characters, reveal information, create conflict, change relationships, or move the plot forward.",
  "tips_screenplay_2_title": "Berikan tujuan pada setiap adegan",
  "tips_screenplay_3_subtitle": "Write action in concise readable paragraphs and include only details that are important for understanding the scene.",
  "tips_screenplay_3_title": "Buat aksi tetap jelas",
  "tips_screenplay_4_subtitle": "Give characters distinct voices and avoid dialogue that exists only to explain information directly to the audience.",
  "tips_screenplay_4_title": "Tulis dialog yang alami",
  "tips_screenplay_5_subtitle": "Start scenes close to the important dramatic moment and finish once the main purpose of the scene is complete.",
  "tips_screenplay_5_title": "Masuk terlambat, keluar lebih awal",
  "tips_screenplay_6_subtitle": "Use actions, reactions, silence, environment, and character choices to make tension visible on screen.",
  "tips_screenplay_6_title": "Ciptakan konflik visual",
  "tips_screenplay_reminder": "A screenplay is meant to be seen and heard. Keep descriptions visual, dialogue purposeful, and every scene easy to imagine.",
  "tips_screenplay_subtitle": "Write visually, keep scenes purposeful, and use concise action and dialogue to create a screenplay that feels cinematic.",
  "tips_screenplay_title": "Tips Menulis Skenario",
  "tips_speech_1_subtitle": "Consider who will listen and adjust your examples, language, humor, tone, and formality to fit that audience.",
  "tips_speech_1_title": "Kenali audiens Anda",
  "tips_speech_2_subtitle": "Begin with a question, short story, surprising idea, or memorable statement that immediately captures attention.",
  "tips_speech_2_title": "Buka dengan kuat",
  "tips_speech_3_subtitle": "Keep the central idea clear throughout the speech so listeners remember what matters most after it ends.",
  "tips_speech_3_title": "Fokus pada satu pesan utama",
  "tips_speech_4_subtitle": "Use natural sentences, conversational wording, pauses, and simple phrasing instead of writing like a formal article.",
  "tips_speech_4_title": "Tulis untuk disampaikan secara lisan",
  "tips_speech_5_subtitle": "Concrete stories and relatable examples make abstract ideas easier for the audience to understand and remember.",
  "tips_speech_5_title": "Gunakan cerita dan contoh",
  "tips_speech_6_subtitle": "End with a strong thought, emotional statement, call to action, or message the audience can carry with them.",
  "tips_speech_6_title": "Akhiri dengan berkesan",
  "tips_speech_reminder": "A speech should sound good aloud. Read it out loud and simplify any sentence that feels unnatural when spoken.",
  "tips_speech_subtitle": "Create speeches that sound natural when spoken, connect with the audience emotionally, and communicate a clear message.",
  "tips_speech_title": "Tips Menulis Pidato",
  "tips_story_1_subtitle": "Open with an interesting moment, mystery, conflict, or question that immediately gives readers a reason to continue.",
  "tips_story_1_title": "Mulai dengan pembuka yang kuat",
  "tips_story_2_subtitle": "Give characters clear goals, motivations, strengths, weaknesses, and emotional reasons behind their decisions.",
  "tips_story_2_title": "Ciptakan karakter yang kuat",
  "tips_story_3_subtitle": "Use obstacles and difficult choices to challenge your characters and naturally move the story forward.",
  "tips_story_3_title": "Ciptakan konflik yang bermakna",
  "tips_story_4_subtitle": "Use actions, dialogue, reactions, and sensory details so readers can experience important moments naturally.",
  "tips_story_4_title": "Tunjukkan, jangan hanya ceritakan",
  "tips_story_5_subtitle": "Balance exciting scenes with quieter emotional moments so the story never feels too rushed or unnecessarily slow.",
  "tips_story_5_title": "Atur tempo cerita",
  "tips_story_6_subtitle": "Resolve the central conflict meaningfully and leave readers with a memorable final emotion, idea, or realization.",
  "tips_story_6_title": "Akhiri dengan kuat",
  "tips_story_reminder": "Every scene should have a purpose. Let it reveal character, deepen emotion, create conflict, or move the story forward.",
  "tips_story_subtitle": "Create engaging stories with memorable characters, meaningful conflict, natural pacing, and a satisfying progression.",
  "tips_story_title": "Tips Menulis Cerita",
